@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About | Legacy Systems Sleuths</PageTitle>

<section class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1>Technical detectives for organizations with inherited mysteries.</h1>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
        <p class="lead">
            Legacy Systems Sleuths is a fictional consulting agency specializing in systems that were built,
            modified, migrated, half-documented, forgotten, and then declared “business critical.”
        </p>

        <p>
            Our philosophy is simple: before recommending a solution, understand the system. That means studying
            workflows, infrastructure, hosting, authentication, documentation, people, and institutional memory.
        </p>

        <p>
            We believe many technical failures are also knowledge failures. A system becomes risky when nobody knows
            who owns it, where it runs, how it is backed up, or why the one spreadsheet is named
            <em>FINAL_final_REAL_USE_THIS_ONE_v7.xlsx</em>.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>